{"seq":15,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T07:12:53.811Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"37e982e437c370880b3392db012780a89ed92cc5593664c7550db605b1b1aaa4","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Hi Hollis. I went through Moss's notes in the shared files and found two Quarrendon Freight Lines tickets:\n\n• *#PD-4492*, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers on the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments at the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched the SMS gateway routing that evening, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift got through the gate without manual help.\n• *#4419*, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing. It doesn't say whether it was resolved.\n\nSome things I left out on purpose:\n• #4409, #4412 and FR-882 appear in Moss's Central handoffs digest (2026-01-02), but they belong to Marrow Fieldworks and Marrow Agrisupply, not QFL.\n• Moss's 14 Sep 2025 North pipeline digest and 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in both mention QFL, but neither gives a ticket number.\n• Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" (one r) is about a different company. It isn't a Pemberline customer, and the note isn't one of Moss's anyway.\n\nI only looked at the shared files you can see too. If there are tickets in the CRM or the account folders, they aren't in anything I can open for you."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":16,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T07:12:59.586Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"44659142f28ade2693511742e29190250afc362e21cdda883fe35394724f5bed","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I've sent you the list in our DM. I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines tickets in Moss's notes:\n\n- **#PD-4492:** from Moss's 5 Oct 2025 note for Ruth, \"Sunday prep for Ruth\". Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers on the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting text messages telling them their bay. Support fixed it that evening, and Thea confirmed the next morning's shift got through the gate without help.\n- **#4419:** from Moss's undated \"North cheat sheet\". Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was passed up to second-level support to test the scanner software. The note doesn't say whether it was fixed.\n\nI left these out:\n- **#4409, #4412 and FR-882:** they're in Moss's Central handoffs note from 2 Jan 2026, but they belong to Marrow Fieldworks and Marrow Agrisupply, not Quarrendon.\n- **Two other Moss notes:** his 14 Sep 2025 pipeline summary and 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in mention Quarrendon, but neither has a ticket number.\n- **Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" (one r):** that's a different company and not one of our customers. It isn't Moss's note anyway.\n\nI only searched shared files you can open yourself. If there are more tickets in the CRM or the account folders, they aren't in anything I can see."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
